1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,636
Is Python interpreted or compiled?

2
00:00:03,006 --> 00:00:04,523
Both. And here's the proof.

3
00:00:04,893 --> 00:00:06,590
First, CPython compiles your

4
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:08,185
source code into bytecode.

5
00:00:08,555 --> 00:00:09,794
You can see it yourself

6
00:00:09,814 --> 00:00:10,889
with the dis module.

7
00:00:11,258 --> 00:00:13,588
Load a. Load b. Add. Return.

8
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:16,042
Then the Python virtual machine

9
00:00:16,062 --> 00:00:17,942
executes those instructions,

10
00:00:17,962 --> 00:00:19,706
one by one, using a stack.

11
00:00:20,076 --> 00:00:22,245
Two goes on the stack. Three goes

12
00:00:22,265 --> 00:00:24,103
on the stack. Add pops both,

13
00:00:24,123 --> 00:00:25,164
and pushes five.

14
00:00:25,534 --> 00:00:26,816
Compiled to bytecode,

15
00:00:26,836 --> 00:00:29,171
then interpreted by a virtual machine.

16
00:00:29,541 --> 00:00:31,768
Follow for more visual explainers on

17
00:00:31,788 --> 00:00:33,391
how software really works.

